 was going to level  off because it gets so hot  have you seen a leveling off absolutely  not  absolutely not it all we've seen here is  an increase and  what i can say in all the years that  i've had personal experience  in dealing with illegal aliens um we  have never dealt with a single family  unit  not a single family unit and the  individuals that are coming through here  i mean there was just a convicted rapist  that was caught not too far from our  property  in route on a trail that was basically  leading him  to our property so absolutely not  actually three nights ago there was a  group at our next door neighbor's house  circling the vehicles and tapping on  their daughter's bedroom window  you said no family units so who are the  people coming across  i mean i can only assume but they're  they're all males there's no females out  on on i mean we live west  of del rio and there's no females out  here there's no children out here and  there are absolutely no family units out  in this way  it's all mostly single males that are  traveling in groups so allison the  people i  we measure are the ones we apprehend or  turn themselves in they get processed  and now they're getting a catch and  release the people you're talking about  aren't getting processed  they're not even being counted yeah  exactly  yeah and if you consider even  what those numbers might be i mean it's  it's unacceptable  there should no one here should be  afraid of you know having their kids  play in their yard or riding their bikes  down the street and none of my neighbors  should be fearful of going out to water  their plants in the morning or the  evening and  being able to sleep at night and what do  you tell local law enforcement  i mean i always thank them because i  mean we personally had a  bailout on our property and because  border patrol couldn't respond because  they were busy processing family units  that day dps responded  so it's just i mean i'm grateful for the  additional support that we're getting  here with  law enforcement i just you know i wish  border patrol was able to go  and do their jobs again and work groups  actively out in the brush and in the  field  what is your message for washington  about  what the reality is living on the border  in texas  it's it's scary i want safety i want  something done  we've been i mean my family personally  has been dealing with illegal immigrants  for years  and nothing's been done and we left a  place  specifically moved to a place peace of  mind and  i mean it's worse here now than where it  was and why we left it's it's worse here  i bet  by the end of this year my encounters  personally will probably surpass  all of those that i dealt with on the  ranch and you got to think that  uh there's some of these people uh have  evil intentions  and unfortunately you're deal you have  to deal with it alone allison anderson  mom of three uh living in texas on the  border that's what your life is like and  it is not right  thanks so much for sharing your story  thank you so much  hi everyone i'm brian kilmeade i want  you to do me a favor i want you to click  to subscribe to the fox news youtube  page  this is the only way that i know for  sure that you're not going to miss any  great commentary  any great news bites any great  interviews coming your way on fox you  can get it all here  on youtube so subscribe right now

